# Cluster-wide Talos and Kubernetes versions.
#
# One consumer: kubernetes/components/common's configMapGenerator turns this
# file into the `cluster-versions` ConfigMap in every namespace, which
# cluster-apps injects into every child HelmRelease/Kustomization as a
# postBuild.substituteFrom source -- making ${KUBERNETES_VERSION} and
# ${TALOS_VERSION} available estate-wide.
#
# The `talos:*` tasks take their versions from talos/topf.yaml, not from here
# -- but `talos:validate-config` CHECKS this file: it fails unless
# KUBERNETES_VERSION and TALOS_VERSION equal topf.yaml's kubernetesVersion /
# talosVersion and tuppr's CRs, and the pinned talosctl matches too.
#
# NOTE: the same two versions are Renovate-managed in THREE places, each with
# its own `# renovate:` annotation, and all three must agree:
#
#   1. this file                                    KUBERNETES_VERSION / TALOS_VERSION
#   2. talos/topf.yaml                              kubernetesVersion / talosVersion
#   3. kubernetes/apps/system-upgrade/upgrades/     tuppr's TalosUpgrade and
#      {talos,kubernetes}.yaml                      KubernetesUpgrade `spec.*.version`
#
# Renovate bumps all three off the same two datasources, so they move
# together. They did not, once: TALOS_VERSION was still v1.13.11 long after
# the cluster ran v1.14.x, because its annotation still named
# ghcr.io/siderolabs/installer -- an image Talos stopped publishing at v1.14.0,
# so Renovate reported it "up to date" forever. Treat any mismatch as a bug.
# Collapsing 3 onto these variables is the obvious follow-up; 2 cannot be
# collapsed, because TOPF reads topf.yaml on a workstation, long before Flux
# substitution ever happens.
#
# Renovate bumps these via the `.env` customManager pattern in
# .github/renovate.json5, which already matches this file.

# renovate: datasource=docker depName=ghcr.io/siderolabs/kubelet
KUBERNETES_VERSION=v1.37.1
# renovate: datasource=github-releases depName=siderolabs/talos
TALOS_VERSION=v1.14.4
